## Statement

Let $A$ be a square matrix with $A^2=0$. Show that $I-A$ is invertible and give its inverse.

## Hint

Multiply $I-A$ by $I+A$.

## Solution

Using $A^2=0$,
$$(I-A)(I+A)=I-A^2=I\qquad\text{and}\qquad(I+A)(I-A)=I-A^2=I.$$

So $I-A$ is invertible and $(I-A)^{-1}=I+A$.
